# Feature-Sliced Design (FSD)

Frontend code lives under `src/` in six layers. Imports may only point **downward**.

```
app → pages → widgets → features → entities → shared
```

## Layers

| Layer | Path | Responsibility |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `app` | `src/app/` | Composition root, providers, global styles |
| `pages` | `src/pages/` | Route-level composition only |
| `widgets` | `src/widgets/` | Composed UI blocks |
| `features` | `src/features/` | User-facing use cases |
| `entities` | `src/entities/` | Domain entities |
| `shared` | `src/shared/` | Swappable infrastructure and UI primitives |

## Import aliases

Always import via aliases — never relative paths across layer boundaries:

`@app`, `@pages`, `@widgets`, `@features`, `@entities`, `@shared`

```ts
// ✅
import { MatchCard } from '@entities/match'
import { Button } from '@shared/ui'
import { ref, greet } from '@shared/api'

// ❌ Direct dependency import
import { invoke } from '@tauri-apps/api/core'
import { ref } from 'vue'

// ❌ Entity imports a feature
import { submitScore } from '@features/scoring'
```

## shared/api

All production runtime dependencies are wrapped as facades under `src/shared/api`. Features/pages/widgets/entities/app import only `@shared/api`.

## Checklist

1. Correct layer chosen?
2. Import direction downward only?
3. Public API exported via `index.ts`?
4. Runtime deps go through `@shared/api`?
5. New UI under `ui/` gets a colocated Storybook story when applicable?
